    "text": "\n000\nFXUS65 KVEF 232357\nAFDVEF\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Las Vegas NV\n357 PM PST Mon Nov 23 2026\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n* Breezy north winds are expected Wednesday and Thursday across\n  the Colorado River Valley. This may result in hazardous boating\n  conditions on large inland lakes.\n\n* A noted warming trend is expected the remainder of the week\n  through the holiday weekend. \n\n* The next substantial storm system looks to impact the Western\n  U.S. the first half of next week.\n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...\nA rather benign weather pattern is expected through the remainder\nof this week and weekend. A pronounced upper ridge will gradually\nbuild in across the Desert Southwest, providing pleasant and mild\nweather conditions. Nights will remain cool, but daytime highs \nwill gradually climb well into the 60s and 70s from Thursday \nthrough Saturday.\n\nOne area of concern will be the Colorado River Valley, where \ngusty north winds look to develop Wednesday through Thanksgiving \nday. This will occur as a shortwave drops south across western \nUtah and Arizona and the pressure gradient tightens in response to\nthe intensifying ridge. At this time, winds appear somewhat \nmarginal for advisory headlines, but they will likely be enough to\ncause problems on large inland lakes. Lake wind and/or wind \nadvisories may become necessary in future forecasts.\n\nBeyond the holiday weekend, ensembles are in generally good \nagreement in the handling of another upper trough emanating from \nthe Eastern Pacific. While details regarding timing and intensity \nremain, the probability of another round of breezy/gusty southwest\nwinds, valley rain and mountain snow is on the rise, particularly\nin the Monday to Wednesday timeframe next week.\n\n&&\n\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 00Z Forecast Package...Mostly\nclear skies and light winds last through the TAF period. Expect \nNortheast winds to turn west-southwest into the night. Winds turn \nnortheast again into mid Tuesday morning but turn west again that \nnight.\n\nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast \nCalifornia...For the 00Z Forecast Package...Mostly clear skies last \nthrough the TAF period. Winds stay light through the night and into \nearly Tuesday, with winds directions being determined by more \nlocalized effects rather than widespread prevailing weather \npatterns. Winds will continue to be light through the rest of the \nTAF period for all but KIFP and KEED, which see breezy northerly \nwinds arrive into Tuesday morning and last into that night.\n&&\n\n.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...Spotters are encouraged to report\nany significant weather or impacts according to standard operating\nprocedures.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...Austin\nAVIATION...Murdock\n\nFor more forecast information...see us on our webpage:\nhttps://weather.gov/lasvegas or follow us on Facebook and Twitter\n",
